  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(\\mathrm{p}^{\\text {th }}, \\mathrm{q}^{\\text {th }}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{r}^{\\text {th }}\\) terms of H.P. are \\(\\mathrm{u}, \\mathrm{v}, \\mathrm{w}\\) respectively, then find the value of the expression \\((q-r) v w+(r-p) w u+(p-q) u v\\)."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "8",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let H.P. be \\(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{d}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}+2 \\mathrm{~d}}+\\ldots \\ldots\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{u}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{p}-1) \\mathrm{d}}, \\mathrm{v}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{q}-1) \\mathrm{d}}, \\\\\n& \\mathrm{w}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{r}-1) \\mathrm{d}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{p}-1) \\mathrm{d}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{u}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{q}-1) \\mathrm{d}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{v}}, \\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{r}-1) \\mathrm{d}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{w}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(\\mathrm{q}-\\mathrm{r})\\{\\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{p}-1) \\mathrm{d}\\}+(\\mathrm{r}-\\mathrm{p})\\{\\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{q}-1) \\mathrm{d}\\}+\\ldots \\ldots \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{u}}(\\mathrm{q}-\\mathrm{r})+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{v}}(\\mathrm{r}-\\mathrm{p})+\\ldots . \\Rightarrow(q-r) \\mathrm{vw}+\\ldots . . = 0\n\\end{aligned}\\)"
  }
}